+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Adreno 735 / Snapdragon 8s Gen 3 (SM8635) — Suyu / Eden notes
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Mesa 24.2+ already registers chip_id 0x43050a as `a735` in the table
+# below. Mesa 26.3.0 inherits that entry and adds the same A7xx Gen4
+# tuning (gmem layout, shaderISDB, LRZ bypass on alpha-test, etc.) that
+# A740/A750 use, because A735 shares the same ISA and rasteriser as the
+# rest of the A7xx family.
+#
+# If a future silicon revision of A735 ships with a chip_id not yet in
+# the table (e.g. 0x43050b), the driver will fall back to the generic
+# "unknown a7xx" path. To force it back to the a735 entry, add:
+#
+#     (0x43050b, A7XX_GEN4, 1 * 1024 * 1024, None, "a735"),
+#
+# to GPU_INFO_TABLE below. This is the ONLY manual edit you should ever
+# need to make for an unreleased A735 revision.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
diff --git a/docs/drivers/freedreno.rst b/docs/drivers/freedreno.rst
--- a/docs/drivers/freedreno.rst
+++ b/docs/drivers/freedreno.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+Adreno 735 (Snapdragon 8s Gen 3 / SM8635)
+=========================================
+
+The A735 is a member of the Adreno 7xx family (A7xx Gen4). Turnip
+enables the full A7xx feature set on this GPU, including:
+
+* VK_EXT_transform_feedback (required by Nintendo Switch emulation)
+* VK_EXT_provoking_vertex (required by Nintendo Switch emulation)
+* VK_EXT_extended_dynamic_state, _state2, _state3
+* VK_EXT_graphics_pipeline_library (fast PSO compiles in Suyu/Eden)
+* VK_KHR_fragment_shading_rate
+* 1 MiB GMEM with conservative binning
